  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Round the cone and in – lay-ups from five angles",
  "description": "Put five cones along the three-point line: both corners, both wings and the top. The player dribbles out with the right hand, round the first cone and back to the basket for a right-hand lay-up. Straight after the finish they grab the ball and move on to the next cone until all five are done. Then the same round again with the left hand – ten lay-ups in total.\n\nTwo players can share a basket if they start at different cones and alternate so only one finishes at a time. With more players, use more baskets. Go at game speed and it doubles as conditioning.\n\nVary it: move the cones elsewhere, make a dribble move at the cone, or finish with a different lay-up (euro step, floater, reverse lay-up). The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Round the cone tightly, then push the ball out in front to speed up towards the basket."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Chin up and eyes on the rim as you go up to finish."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Drive your knee high on the take-off – it gives you height and control."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Full speed all the way, as in a game."
    }
  ],
